# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository *and* in the working tree.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `bin/pixelproof.mjs` starts with `#!/usr/bin/env node`,
# and a shebang followed by CR is not a shebang: the kernel takes the CR as part
# of the interpreter path and the exec fails with "bad interpreter". Git already
# stores LF; without `eol=lf` a Windows checkout converts it to CRLF and ships a
# broken executable — which a Windows working tree cannot notice, because the
# file it was written with is fine and only a fresh clone shows the difference.
#
# Forcing LF on checkout keeps every clone byte-identical to the index, on every
# platform, so this class of bug cannot come back.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
